    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if we stop looking at it through a purely medical lens and look at it through the lens of evolutionary biology... it almost seems like a natural way for the species to prepare for a massive shift. a way to create a layer of high-functioning individuals who can process reality at a much higher resolution. if someone was actually experiencing this, would it make sense to view them as a prototype for what comes next, rather than just a \"cognitive outlier\"?",
